  "limits": [
    "Only two existing Chinese/English synthetic short phrases. Small samples, sequential nonrandomized variants; no P95 or broad travel-language claim.",
    "End of speech estimated from Silero samples_index minus silence_duration, mapped to a 100ms PCM send frame; not a physical last-phoneme measurement.",
    "Downstream is loopback, excluding phone-network delay, production business HTTP authentication, and concurrent load.",
    "Android measures silent PCM write to observed playback-head progress with a 2ms poll, not physical speaker sound or real translated-audio arrival.",
    "Server and Android measurements are separate clocks/runs; do not add them into an asserted end-to-end latency.",
    "Negative end-relative provider latency is retained when the model streams audio before the estimated speech end.",
    "Preliminary reports precede output-item correlation; use the correlated baseline as the primary comparison. Preserve the single original TranslationError with unknown root cause.",
    "Background cleanup is a diagnostic-only experiment. It disables speculative preparation and awaits retirement on teardown; no production runtime changed.",
    "No phone-direct transport or real phone-network A/B was measured; cannot quantify the gain of migrating to direct WSS.",
    "Human voice/listening, mixed languages, short ambiguous words, headset routes and true end-to-acoustic latency remain pending because the user was unavailable.",
    "All prior CPU/gray-rollout/headphone/concurrency/invoice scope decisions remain in force."
